# Security Rules

## Never

- Commit secrets, API keys, private keys, webhook secrets
- Log passwords, access/refresh tokens, payment credentials, unnecessary sensitive PII
- Trust the client for entitlements, premium flags, or `reward=true`
- Expose permanent public URLs for paid media
- Disable authz checks “temporarily” in production paths

## Always

- Validate/sanitize inputs at API boundary
- Enforce RBAC + ownership checks server-side
- Use short-lived signed URLs for entitled media
- Rate-limit auth, checkout, SSV, upload
- Audit admin grants, refunds, config changes
- Verify payment webhooks and AdMob SSV signatures

## Uploads

Allowlist MIME · size limits · checksum · async malware scan hook
